Package: sideview
Title: Explore and Join Many Tables on a Zoomable Canvas
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yee How", "Lau", email = "lauyeehow1986@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
  )
Description: Lays out many data frames side by side as cards on a pan-and-zoom
    canvas, either as a 'shiny' gadget for 'RStudio' or as an 'htmlwidgets'
    widget for 'R Markdown' and 'Quarto' pages. Drawing a line between two
    columns writes the 'dplyr' join and checks it first: match rates, unmatched
    keys and the key relationship. Sorts, filters and other steps build up a
    readable pipeline of R code, and a column inspector exports a data
    dictionary. An optional large language model (LLM) assistant, using
    'Ollama' or an 'OpenAI'-compatible service, suggests 'tidyverse' code from
    the table schema only, never the data rows.
URL: https://lauyeehow1986-hub.github.io/sideview/, https://github.com/lauyeehow1986-hub/sideview
BugReports: https://github.com/lauyeehow1986-hub/sideview/issues
